--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Hardware encoder runtime (container image, linux/amd64 only)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The amd64 image also REDISTRIBUTES the VAAPI and QSV userspace, copied out of
Debian 13 (trixie) binary packages: libva, libva-drm and libdrm (which the bundled
ffmpeg loads for any VAAPI or QSV device), Intel's iHD VA driver and libmfx-gen
(the QSV runtime), Mesa's radeonsi VA driver for AMD, and the shared libraries
those need. The arm64 image carries none of it.

Each package below is pinned in the Dockerfile (hwruntime stage) by this exact
version and by the sha256 of its .deb, and fetched from snapshot.debian.org at
the snapshot the Dockerfile names. Only its shared objects are copied (from
mesa-va-drivers only radeonsi_drv_video.so; from libdrm-common only
/usr/share/libdrm/amdgpu.ids), together with its Debian copyright file, which the
image carries at /usr/share/doc/<package>/copyright. That file is the complete
licence statement; the licence named here is a summary of it, read from the file
of the pinned version on 2026-09-30. scripts/check-pins.sh fails when the
packages below and the Dockerfile's pins disagree, in name or version, in either
direction.

  Corresponding source: every package below was built by Debian from the source
  package named on its "source:" line, at that version, and snapshot.debian.org
  keeps that source (the .dsc, the upstream tarball and the Debian changes) at
  the URL on the same line, permanently. That is the corresponding source for the
  GPL- and LGPL-licensed members of this set (libelf1t64, libsensors5, and the
  GPL-licensed files other copyright files list), and for every other package too.

  Non-free: intel-media-va-driver-non-free is in Debian's non-free section. Its
  licence is Expat and BSD-3-clause and Debian redistributes it; it is non-free
  under the Debian Free Software Guidelines because it contains prebuilt GPU
  kernels without their source ("we have to move those kernels to non-free as
  they come without source", its Debian copyright file). It is the full-feature
  build of the Intel driver; the free build lacks HEVC encode on parts older than
  Ice Lake. The source package linked below is what Debian distributes; it
  contains those kernels as binaries.

  Not carried: AMD's AMF runtime (libamfrt64). Its licence, the AMDGPU PRO EULA,
  grants no redistribution, so `encoder: amf` cannot work in this image; AMD
  hardware encodes here through `encoder: vaapi`.

